{"id":507,"name":"herdier","speciesId":507,"dex":507,"form":"normal","generation":5,"types":["normal"],"stats":{"hp":65,"attack":80,"defense":65,"special-attack":35,"special-defense":65,"speed":60},"abilities":[{"name":"intimidate","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-rush","hidden":false},{"name":"scrappy","hidden":true}],"height":9,"weight":147,"baseExp":130,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/507.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/507.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/507.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/507.ogg","genus":"Loyal Dog Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon cão leal","flavor":[{"version":"black","text":"It has black, cape-like fur that is very hard and decreases the amount of damage it receives."},{"version":"white","text":"It loyally follows its Trainer’s orders. For ages, they have helped Trainers raise Pokémon."},{"version":"black-2","text":"This very loyal Pokémon helps Trainers, and it also takes care of other Pokémon."},{"version":"sun","text":"Its dense black fur grows continuously. The high cost of keeping its hard fur properly groomed makes this a troublesome Pokémon to train."},{"version":"moon","text":"This Pokémon obeys its master’s orders faithfully. However, it refuses to listen to anything said by a person it doesn’t respect."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"The longer its black fur grows, the harder and more impervious it gets. Claws and fangs can’t easily penetrate it."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It has been living with people for so long that portrayals of it can be found on the walls of caves from long, long ago."},{"version":"sword","text":"Herdier is a very smart and friendly Pokémon. So much so that there’s a theory that Herdier was the first Pokémon to partner with people."},{